hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17943","Harun narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Abu Ushshanah narrated to him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say, I will not say today about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, Whoever lies about me what I did not say, let him take a house in Hell."
"17944","And I heard the Prophet say, Two men of my nation: one rises at night striving with himself to purify, with knots upon him. So he performs ablution; when he washes his hands a knot is loosened, and when he washes his face a knot is loosened, and when he wipes his head a knot is loosened, and when he washes his feet a knot is loosened. So Allah Almighty says to those behind the veil, Look at this servant of Mine striving with himself, asking Me; whatever My servant asks of Me is his."
"17945","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Hunayn ibn Abi Hakim, he narrated to him, from Ali ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to recite the Muawwidhat at the end of every prayer."
"17946","Affan narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, he said, My sister vowed to walk to the Kabah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Allah is free of her walking; let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel."
"17947","Affan narrated to us, he said, Aban informed us, he said, Qatadah narrated to us, he said, Nuaym ibn Hammar narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Your Lord said, Are you unable, O son of Adam, to pray four rakahs at the start of the day, I will suffice you with them at the end of your day."
"17948","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to me, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani, he said, Uqbah ibn Amir accompanied us on a journey but would not lead us. So we said to him, May Allah have mercy on you, will you not lead us though you are of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said, No, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, Whoever leads the people, and gets the time right and completes the prayer, he has reward and they have reward. And whoever falls short of that, the burden is upon him and not upon them."
"17949","Abu Abd al-Rahman said, I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting: al-Rabi ibn Nafi Abu Tawbah wrote to me, and in his book: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, One who recites the Quran secretly is like one who gives charity secretly, and one who recites the Quran aloud is like one who gives charity aloud."
